摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"An enterprise workbench for the DeepSeek Harness: AI employees, knowledge bases, skills, MCP servers and DSH plugins, all manageable from a running session.","id":"gh:1342911130","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-workbench","slug":"staff-os/dsh-workbench","topics":["agent-framework","agent-skill","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","enterprise-ai","enterprise-ai-engineering","skillhub"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"An enterprise workbench for the DeepSeek Harness: AI employees, knowledge bases, skills, MCP servers"},{"id":"p1s2","text":" and DSH plugins, all manageable from a running session."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# @staff-os/dsh-workbench"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Enterprise workbench plugin for DeepSeek Harness: **AI employees, knowledge bases, skills, MCP\nserve"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"rs, DSH plugins** — five domains, each with a tool for the model and a management surface for\nthe pe"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"SH plugins** — five domains, each with a tool for the model and a management surface for\nthe person."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"**Runs standalone.** No external backend, no database. Every piece of state is a local file under\n`$"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"ndalone.** No external backend, no database. Every piece of state is a local file under\n`$DSH_HOME`."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## What it does"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"### Skills"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Local skills live under `$DSH_HOME/skills`, one directory per `SKILL.md`; they can also be installed"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"\nfrom a configured marketplace. The inventory leads with three counts — how many this plugin manages"},{"id":"p8s3","text":",\nhow many are **shadowed** by a same-named higher-priority source, and how many DSH **rejected whol"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"e**\nover non-compliant frontmatter. The last two both present in a session as \"I installed it but it"},{"id":"p8s5","text":"\nnever fires\", and DSH itself only logs one warning line about them."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"After every write the plugin reads `ctx.skills` back, so what it reports is whether the skill is in\n"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"effect *now* — not \"after a restart\". Once the file lands, the next model turn has it."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"The marketplace aggregates several sources, and each card names the one it came from. A blank browse"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"\nis sorted by total downloads; a keyword search keeps the order the marketplace returned. Cards carr"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"y\nno install button — the whole card opens the detail, because installing a skill is not installing "},{"id":"p10s4","text":"a\nlibrary: the body of a SKILL.md is instructions the model will follow, and what you need in order "},{"id":"p10s5","text":"to\ndecide (publisher, review verdict, package contents, static scan) is in there."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"The detail has three tabs: **overview** renders the SKILL.md (with a raw-source toggle), **files** i"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"s\nthe package's directory tree with in-place previews, and **security scan** is thirteen regex rules"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"\nplus a charset-smuggling check. The rule set is ported from the skill-scan pre-check in Tencent Zhu"},{"id":"p11s4","text":"que\nLab's AI-Infra-Guard (Apache-2.0). A match only means the\ntext looks like a high-risk pattern, n"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"ot that it does it — and no match does not mean safe."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Import takes four sources — an archive, a download link, a GitHub repository, a marketplace slug —\no"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"ver one unpack-and-land path: staged outside the skill root first, swapped in as a whole directory\no"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"nce it checks out. Only the marketplace slug gets a ledger entry, which is how later update checks\nf"},{"id":"p12s4","text":"ind their way back to the same source by id."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"### AI employees"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"An employee is a DSH agent preset. Discovery, trust level, copying and deletion all go through the\nn"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"ative `ctx.agentPresets`: creating one is a **whole-directory copy** of an existing preset, so a cop"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"y\nnever carries more capability than its source, and a `system`-trust preset ships with the deployme"},{"id":"p14s4","text":"nt\nand can be neither edited nor deleted. Bindings live in `employee.yml` inside the preset director"},{"id":"p14s5","text":"y and\nare a **statement of responsibility, not autowiring** — binding a knowledge base does not make"},{"id":"p14s6","text":"\nretrieval happen. The UI lives in `client/employee/`; its entry point is hidden for now."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"### Knowledge bases"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Local chunking plus a keyword index; retrieval is BM25, not semantic vectors. Text only."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"### MCP servers"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Written into the current profile's patch file; **changes take effect on the next DSH start**.\n`impor"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"t_json` accepts the Claude Code / Cursor shape `{\"mcpServers\": {...}}` and rewrites `${VAR}`\ninto `!"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"!js process.env.VAR` — DSH does no client-side environment substitution, so without the\nrewrite the "},{"id":"p18s4","text":"server receives the literal fifteen characters `${GITHUB_TOKEN}`."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"### DSH plugins"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Forwarded to the `dsh plugin` CLI; this plugin never touches pnpm or edits `dsh.profile.bundles`\nits"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"elf. `list` splits \"does this package declare `dsh.bundle`\" from \"is it in the composition layer\" —\n"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"after an install, only those two together say whether it really became a plugin."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"For local development, use an absolute path:"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Restart DSH afterwards."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Configure"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"The bundled `cordis.patch.yml` is an opt-in patch layer that reads its config from the environment\nb"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"d `cordis.patch.yml` is an opt-in patch layer that reads its config from the environment\nby default:"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"| Variable | Effect |"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"| `DSH_PROFILE` | Which profile MCP and plugin management act on. Defaults to `web` |\n| `CLAWHUB_REG"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"ISTRY` | Root URL of a ClawHub-compatible marketplace. Unset falls back to the shipped one (public r"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"ead endpoints, no token) |\n| `CLAWHUB_API_KEY` | Marketplace credential. **A reference name only** —"},{"id":"p29s4","text":" the value is resolved from the credential service or the launch environment, never inlined into YAM"},{"id":"p29s5","text":"e value is resolved from the credential service or the launch environment, never inlined into YAML |"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"Environment variables go in `$DSH_HOME/.env` or the `.env` beside wherever `dsh` is invoked; both\nla"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"yers are read at startup."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"To point at a self-hosted marketplace, edit the profile's own patch layer\n(`$DSH_HOME/profiles/<name"},{"id":"p31s2","text":">/cordis.patch.yml`) rather than the environment: the environment path can\nonly swap the URL, while "},{"id":"p31s3","text":"`id` and display name stay fixed, leaving the UI labelling an intranet\nsource \"ClawHub\". The patch l"},{"id":"p31s4","text":"ayer hot-reloads, so no restart:"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"`flavor` has exactly two values: `clawhub` (the default, and any ClawHub-compatible deployment) and\n"},{"id":"p33s2","text":"`skillhub` (deployments that split browsing into `/api/v1/showcase/*` leaderboard endpoints and\nansw"},{"id":"p33s3","text":"er 405 on `/api/v1/skills`)."},{"id":"p34s1","text":"Skill marketplace sources can also be added and removed from the UI. Those land in\n`$DSH_HOME/workbe"},{"id":"p34s2","text":"nch/market.json`, take effect immediately, and never enter the Cordis config; an\nempty file falls ba"},{"id":"p34s3","text":"ck to what is configured here."},{"id":"p35s1","text":"## Structure"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"One Cordis plugin, contributing at three mount points:"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"| Mount point | What goes there |"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"| `ctx.tools` | Five tools, one per domain, with an `action` parameter. **Destructive actions requir"},{"id":"p38s2","text":"e an explicit `confirm: true`** or they return an error and write nothing |\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
